s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-06-23T09:34:25Z","updated_at":"2025-06-24T15:12:13Z","closed_at":"2025-06-24T15:10:45Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107886","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107886.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107886.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-24T15:10:45Z"},"body":"Also fixup FTI configuration warnings so that they only output when the project is using FTI.\r\n\r\n@BastiaanOlij noticed that some FTI configuration warnings were firing when FTI was off in the project.\r\nThis happened because checking whether FTI was on in the editor was previously unsupported (as it was hard coded to OFF).\r\n\r\nI had also been long term intending to swap using a local variable for global on / off in `SceneTree` to a static, the reason being that it would no longer be necessary to check `is_inside_tree()` and access the variable via a pointer, for what is likely to be a bottleneck check (and the global setting hardly ever changes, so a static makes sense here).\r\n\r\nSo I take the opportunity to swap both the global setting to a static, and add an extra one for checking the on / off setting within the editor (while not actually enabled the FTI functionality).\r\n\r\nThis enables us to check the project global setting before issuing configuration warnings, without having to use e.g. `GET_GLOBAL_CACHED()`, which isn't a particularly good way of doing this here due to the string duplication.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n* Also applicable to 3.x.\r\n* I also want to actually get an MRP for the scene tree that caused this warning, just in case there is some pattern used in XR that won't well with the FTI, but that is a separate issue.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/contributing/development/code_style_guidelines.html\r\n-->\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107886/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_re